WEBVTT

00:11.490 --> 00:13.530
<b>I'm sorry, Brother.</b>

00:13.530 --> 00:16.530
<b>I was reminiscing a bit about the past.</b>

00:16.990 --> 00:18.370
<b>Were they fun memories?</b>

00:19.740 --> 00:21.120
<b>No.</b>

00:22.040 --> 00:25.000
<b>Back then, I was so foolish.</b>

00:25.750 --> 00:27.420
<b>And it seems so comical.</b>

00:29.750 --> 00:32.880
<b>Even though I'm your little sister...</b>

00:32.880 --> 00:36.760
<b>I didn't have a single clue about you.</b>

00:37.510 --> 00:38.510
<b>No.</b>

00:38.890 --> 00:40.930
<b>I didn't even try to understand.</b>

00:42.270 --> 00:43.560
<b>Miyuki...</b>

02:21.120 --> 02:22.740
<b>APRIL 13, A.D. 2096</b>

02:25.740 --> 02:27.500
<b>Please join the track team!</b>

02:25.740 --> 02:27.500
<b>WELCOMING
INEXPERIENCED
PEOPLE</b>

02:34.090 --> 02:37.260
<b>The recruitment process
sure is peaceful this year.</b>

02:37.260 --> 02:39.760
<b>Yes. I just hope nothing happens.</b>

02:40.800 --> 02:42.300
<b>Right.</b>

02:43.430 --> 02:45.890
<b>Still, who would've thought?</b>

02:46.220 --> 02:49.640
<b>Last year, I was this close
to being suspended for causing an uproar...</b>

02:49.980 --> 02:53.020
<b>but this year, I'm on the side
that cracks down on uproars.</b>

02:53.690 --> 02:56.900
<b>Kirihara, would you mind
not talking about that?</b>

02:57.480 --> 02:59.950
<b>Someone might get the wrong idea,
and it would mean trouble.</b>

03:01.110 --> 03:02.660
<b>You're ignoring me?</b>

03:04.580 --> 03:06.540
<b>Yes? Extracurricular Activities Federation.</b>

03:09.040 --> 03:10.790
<b>Is that right? Understood.</b>

03:14.290 --> 03:15.960
<b>Shiba, Ms. Shiba...</b>

03:16.500 --> 03:17.380
<b>Yes?</b>

03:17.380 --> 03:20.130
<b>We have a situation
in the Robot Research Club's garage.</b>

03:20.420 --> 03:21.720
<b>Could you go mediate?</b>

03:22.340 --> 03:24.090
<b>- Understood.
- Understood.</b>

03:24.090 --> 03:26.600
<b>ROBOT RESEARCH CLUB
WELCOME NEWCOMERS</b>

03:27.180 --> 03:29.600
<b>Just give it up already!</b>

03:29.600 --> 03:32.140
<b>This kid says he wants to join
the Robot Research Club!</b>

03:32.690 --> 03:37.900
<b>We called out to him first,
so would you mind not butting in?</b>

03:37.900 --> 03:39.530
<b>Uh... I...</b>

03:39.860 --> 03:42.780
<b>Robot Research Club, Motorcycle Club...
Both of you settle down!</b>

03:42.780 --> 03:44.910
<b>I'm from the Extracurricular Activities
Federation. What's the problem?</b>

03:44.910 --> 03:46.410
<b>Hey, out of the way!</b>

03:48.410 --> 03:50.040
<b>I'm with the Disciplinary Committee.</b>

03:50.960 --> 03:54.170
<b>The Extracurricular Activities Federation
is handling this already.</b>

03:54.790 --> 03:56.670
<b>Get lost, Disciplinary Committee.</b>

03:57.130 --> 04:01.470
<b>But I'd say that disputes between students
is the purview of the Disciplinary Committee.</b>

04:02.680 --> 04:03.880
<b>Hey, hold up!</b>

04:07.930 --> 04:10.430
<b>So persistent!
Stay out of my way, will you?</b>

04:10.770 --> 04:13.980
<b>We told you we'd deal with this, Saegusa.</b>

04:13.980 --> 04:16.810
<b>Or wait, maybe you need to have it
spelled out to get it?</b>

04:17.360 --> 04:19.400
<b>This is none of your business!</b>

04:19.400 --> 04:21.150
<b>I hate to break it to you...</b>

04:21.150 --> 04:25.570
<b>but the Disciplinary Committee
is under no obligation to do your bidding!</b>

04:26.410 --> 04:28.830
<b>Are you picking a fight with me, Saegusa?</b>

04:29.620 --> 04:31.580
<b>Not my intention at all.</b>

04:31.580 --> 04:34.000
<b>Though I'm not at all loath to fight!</b>

04:34.420 --> 04:35.540
<b>Oh?</b>

04:35.920 --> 04:39.840
<b>So, a Saegusa's going to take on
a Shippou's challenge to fight?</b>

04:40.170 --> 04:44.470
<b>Sure, I'll take up the gauntlet
for the beatdown you're offering.</b>

04:44.470 --> 04:47.600
<b>When I'm done, you'll never think
about picking a fight with me again!</b>

04:47.890 --> 04:50.970
<b>Your other half's not here.
Will you be okay on your own?</b>

04:50.970 --> 04:54.020
<b>What, you want an excuse for losing?</b>

04:54.480 --> 04:56.100
<b>Hold up! Calm down!</b>

05:02.570 --> 05:04.740
<b>Both of you, what are you doing?</b>

05:07.870 --> 05:09.740
<b>The Federation and the Disciplinary Committee...</b>

05:09.740 --> 05:13.120
<b>tasked with governing the students, fighting
among each other? What's the meaning of this?</b>

05:13.950 --> 05:16.960
<b>- We apologize for causing a commotion!
- We apologize for causing a commotion!</b>

05:17.750 --> 05:21.250
<b>We're going to look the other way this time,
but there won't be a next time.</b>

05:21.250 --> 05:23.590
<b>Both of you, get back to work.</b>

05:24.050 --> 05:28.840
<b>I believe that the rest of you should also
go back to doing what you were doing.</b>

05:29.470 --> 05:33.100
<b>The Student Council will not pursue
this case any further.</b>

05:33.720 --> 05:38.190
<b>As for the Disciplinary Committee and the Federation,
I'll make things right on my end.</b>

05:44.860 --> 05:48.740
<b>So, as you can see,
he was totally annoying.</b>

05:49.110 --> 05:52.030
<b>Good for you for controlling
yourself, Kasumi.</b>

05:52.700 --> 05:55.290
<b>Yeah, well...</b>

05:55.870 --> 05:59.290
<b>But if I'm being honest,
I really wanted to blast him away!</b>

05:59.880 --> 06:04.800
<b>Still, Shippou's behavior
is altogether too unfriendly, right?</b>

06:05.300 --> 06:08.550
<b>Unfriendly is putting it mildly.</b>

06:08.550 --> 06:10.930
<b>That's called belligerence!</b>

06:11.350 --> 06:12.510
<b>All right.</b>

06:12.850 --> 06:15.810
<b>So, about that belligerent attitude...</b>

06:15.810 --> 06:20.230
<b>to say that the Extracurricular Activities Federation
was being hostile to the Disciplinary Committee...</b>

06:20.230 --> 06:22.690
<b>doesn't go far enough to explain it, right?</b>

06:23.230 --> 06:24.570
<b>That's right.</b>

06:24.570 --> 06:28.200
<b>He was picking a fight
as a Shippou with a Saegusa!</b>

06:28.780 --> 06:34.200
<b>Whether or not it was as a Saegusa,
he did seem to have some personal animosity.</b>

06:35.290 --> 06:38.080
<b>You mean a personal grudge?</b>

06:39.120 --> 06:44.130
<b>I hear that the current head
of the Shippou Family is gentle by nature.</b>

06:44.880 --> 06:49.340
<b>I doubt he'd ever provoke us directly.</b>

06:55.390 --> 06:56.470
<b>Come in.</b>

07:02.940 --> 07:05.190
<b>Did you get to the bottom of it, Nakura?</b>

07:05.190 --> 07:05.980
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

07:06.360 --> 07:09.700
<b>The New Breed Front,
which occupied the offshore tower...</b>

07:09.700 --> 07:12.530
<b>was collaborating with FAIR.</b>

07:13.200 --> 07:14.240
<b>FAIR?</b>

07:14.580 --> 07:18.200
<b>A magician supremacist extremist group
from America, right?</b>

07:18.540 --> 07:19.250
<b>But...</b>

07:19.830 --> 07:23.130
<b>I thought the offshore tower
was a model case...</b>

07:23.500 --> 07:26.750
<b>exhibiting magicians being involved in security
as humans and not as weapons.</b>

07:27.760 --> 07:30.130
<b>Why did they try to destroy it?</b>

07:30.590 --> 07:35.850
<b>Because their aim isn't to see magicians
and humans existing hand in hand.</b>

07:37.470 --> 07:38.850
<b>But even so...</b>

07:38.850 --> 07:44.100
<b>if they trample on the hopes of so many magicians,
there's sure to be internal discord.</b>

07:44.650 --> 07:46.610
<b>And criticism aimed at the organization.</b>

07:47.480 --> 07:50.360
<b>Why would they take such rash action?</b>

07:51.200 --> 07:56.870
<b>It would seem that there's a USNA humanist
among their top players.</b>

07:59.200 --> 08:01.750
<b>By having a giant monument
such as the offshore tower...</b>

08:01.750 --> 08:04.750
<b>be destroyed by the New Breed Front...</b>

08:04.750 --> 08:08.880
<b>they were surely trying to broadcast
the danger of magicians to the world.</b>

08:10.970 --> 08:13.010
<b>Fine. Step back.</b>

08:20.930 --> 08:24.140
<b>It's me. Let me talk to Mr. Kudou.</b>

08:26.190 --> 08:28.520
<b>So, what did you want to talk to me about?</b>

08:29.070 --> 08:33.240
<b>Big Sister, do you know what kind of person
the head of the Shippou Family is?</b>

08:34.990 --> 08:36.240
<b>Kasumi...</b>

08:37.620 --> 08:39.240
<b>Wh-What is it?</b>

08:39.740 --> 08:43.000
<b>You caused some trouble
with Shippou, didn't you?</b>

08:44.870 --> 08:46.250
<b>How did you find out?</b>

08:47.080 --> 08:48.420
<b>Look, you...</b>

08:48.920 --> 08:50.800
<b>Please hold on a minute, Sister.</b>

08:51.130 --> 08:54.050
<b>Regarding the incident today...</b>

08:54.380 --> 08:58.350
<b>you could say it was Shippou
who was more to blame than Kasumi.</b>

09:05.390 --> 09:07.770
<b>Fine. I'll trust what you say.</b>

09:11.320 --> 09:15.820
<b>So, you wanted to know what kind
of personality the Shippou head has.</b>

09:15.820 --> 09:16.860
<b>Yes.</b>

09:17.360 --> 09:18.160
<b>Let's see.</b>

09:19.700 --> 09:22.830
<b>Not that I have any firsthand knowledge...</b>

09:23.200 --> 09:25.790
<b>but I think he's dependable and thorough.</b>

09:26.370 --> 09:29.080
<b>Dependable and thorough?</b>

09:29.080 --> 09:30.000
<b>Right.</b>

09:30.540 --> 09:34.720
<b>He'll formulate multiple strategies,
keep risks to the minimum...</b>

09:34.720 --> 09:38.260
<b>try not to reap too much,
and securely get his money's worth.</b>

09:38.840 --> 09:40.550
<b>That's the type of person he is.</b>

09:40.550 --> 09:42.010
<b>But doesn't that mean...</b>

09:42.600 --> 09:48.770
<b>Yes. It seems like the total opposite
of how Shippou was acting toward you.</b>

09:49.190 --> 09:52.150
<b>So, it is a personal grudge
against me after all?</b>

09:52.690 --> 09:54.740
<b>Can you think of a reason?</b>

09:54.740 --> 09:55.860
<b>Nope.</b>

09:56.490 --> 10:00.620
<b>But if he ever tries to pull something on me,
I'm so going to destroy him first!</b>

10:00.620 --> 10:02.540
<b>Kasumi!</b>

10:08.790 --> 10:09.880
<b>Huh?</b>

10:10.540 --> 10:12.590
<b>I'm sorry!</b>

10:15.920 --> 10:18.630
<b>I apologize for calling so late, sir.</b>

10:19.180 --> 10:20.640
<b><i>It's fine.</i></b>

10:20.640 --> 10:22.470
<b>Thank you very much.</b>

10:23.060 --> 10:25.100
<b><i>I've just received word...</i></b>

10:25.100 --> 10:34.780
<b><i>that the USNA's humanists are planning
a negative press campaign against magicians.</i></b>

10:34.780 --> 10:35.730
<b>Oh?</b>

10:36.110 --> 10:40.240
<b>Apparently, the manipulation of information
is already gaining traction.</b>

10:41.070 --> 10:44.870
<b>I'm sure you knew about this
before today.</b>

10:45.740 --> 10:47.500
<b><i>You've seen right through me, then?</i></b>

10:48.660 --> 10:51.000
<b>So, what are you planning?</b>

10:51.830 --> 10:54.500
<b>The Yotsubas have too much power.</b>

10:54.500 --> 10:59.510
<b>Before long, they could even disrupt the balance
between the Ten Master Clans and the nation.</b>

11:00.340 --> 11:03.180
<b><i>Do you not agree, Your Excellency?</i></b>

11:03.970 --> 11:09.190
<b>You're going to use the anti-magic faction
to diminish the Yotsubas' power, then?</b>

11:09.770 --> 11:14.980
<b><i>A student with close ties to the 101 Battalion
is enrolled at First High.</i></b>

11:14.980 --> 11:18.190
<b><i>The collusion between this teenaged boy's
high school and the military...</i></b>

11:18.820 --> 11:23.450
<b>The media and the humanist politicians
would favor such a storyline, don't you think?</b>

11:24.240 --> 11:28.080
<b>But your own daughters
attend First High, as well.</b>

11:28.330 --> 11:33.710
<b>I am emphasizing the link between
the 101 Battalion and the Yotsubas.</b>

11:35.460 --> 11:37.800
<b>Is that what you're after?</b>

11:37.800 --> 11:39.590
<b><i>Your thoughts, Your Excellency?</i></b>

11:40.220 --> 11:43.720
<b>I believe that approving
a limited negative campaign...</b>

11:43.720 --> 11:47.970
<b>will allow the anti-magic trend
to lose steam.</b>

11:47.970 --> 11:50.560
<b><i>Their target is still a high school student.</i></b>

11:50.560 --> 11:56.110
<b><i>If we handle this right, we might even be able
to direct the public's ire toward the anti-magic faction.</i></b>

11:56.730 --> 12:00.570
<b>I believe this plan would have merit
for the Ten Master Clans.</b>

12:02.490 --> 12:06.450
<b>I don't have the authority
to approve your plan.</b>

12:07.160 --> 12:10.450
<b>No authority, maybe,
but you do possess influence.</b>

12:10.960 --> 12:13.960
<b>I am not against your plan.</b>

12:14.630 --> 12:17.960
<b><i>That's sufficient.
Thank you very much.</i></b>

12:17.960 --> 12:19.300
<b><i>Excuse me.</i></b>

12:33.480 --> 12:35.020
<b>THE IRREGULAR
AT MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
DOUBLE SEVEN PART II</b>

12:35.650 --> 12:38.020
<b>APRIL 14, A.D. 2096</b>

12:38.860 --> 12:42.240
<b>Big Brother Tatsuya, Big Sister Miyuki,
long time no see.</b>

12:42.700 --> 12:44.610
<b>It's been a long time since we've seen you.</b>

12:45.700 --> 12:47.780
<b>We apologize for coming over so late.</b>

12:48.120 --> 12:50.240
<b>Why are you here in Tokyo today?</b>

12:50.910 --> 12:55.250
<b>I didn't think the Kanto region
was your territory, Fumiya.</b>

12:55.790 --> 13:00.250
<b>Actually, there's something
I wanted to let you both know.</b>

13:01.010 --> 13:06.640
<b>At this time, anti-magician forces
are starting to manipulate the media.</b>

13:08.600 --> 13:09.760
<b>From where?</b>

13:10.260 --> 13:12.890
<b>The USNA humanists.</b>

13:15.270 --> 13:18.730
<b>An anti-magician campaign
through the media?</b>

13:19.110 --> 13:20.980
<b>It's not just the media.</b>

13:20.980 --> 13:23.320
<b>They've also approached
members of Parliament.</b>

13:24.820 --> 13:27.070
<b>- Tell me more about this.
- Right.</b>

13:27.870 --> 13:33.540
<b>First, they criticize the military's use of magicians
on the pretext of defending their human rights.</b>

13:34.580 --> 13:39.920
<b>Next, based on the fact that a quarter
of Magic University graduates serve in the military...</b>

13:39.920 --> 13:46.300
<b>they create a false narrative that the magic
education institutions are colluding with the military.</b>

13:46.300 --> 13:47.930
<b>In the third phase...</b>

13:47.930 --> 13:53.720
<b>they call for the liberation of the children
about to be exploited by the military...</b>

13:53.720 --> 13:58.100
<b>focusing on First High, which is known to send
the most graduates to the Magic Universities.</b>

13:58.560 --> 14:02.730
<b>That's their scenario
as far as we know at this time.</b>

14:03.400 --> 14:05.610
<b>I'm impressed that you were able
to dig so deep.</b>

14:06.360 --> 14:07.820
<b>Oh, uh...</b>

14:07.820 --> 14:09.990
<b>Thank you very much.</b>

14:11.120 --> 14:13.290
<b>I'll try to think of a countermeasure myself.</b>

14:13.830 --> 14:16.870
<b>If anything comes up,
let me hear your follow-up report.</b>

14:16.870 --> 14:18.540
<b>Understood!</b>

14:19.170 --> 14:21.540
<b>APRIL 18, A.D. 2096
NATIONAL MAGIC UNIVERSITY</b>

14:24.130 --> 14:26.550
<b>Thank you for waiting, Jumonji!</b>

14:27.170 --> 14:29.260
<b>Hey, sorry to make you
come all this way, Saegusa.</b>

14:30.010 --> 14:31.470
<b>Don't give it second thought.</b>

14:31.470 --> 14:36.140
<b>It must be really urgent
for you to summon me, Jumonji.</b>

14:39.350 --> 14:41.060
<b><i>A soundproof field?</i></b>

14:42.060 --> 14:44.070
<b>Is it that important?</b>

14:44.860 --> 14:49.570
<b>Starting from this week, there's been a surge
in anti-magician reporting by the media.</b>

14:49.570 --> 14:52.580
<b>3 hours ago
This is the truth!
The reality of magicians
being used for militaristic purposes
5 hours ago
"We can't choose our own future."
Young magicians drafted to the SDF</b>

14:49.570 --> 14:52.580
<b>1 hour ago
Magicians are a privileged class
Magician Officers are favored
2 hours ago
Which one has more power?
Magicians are controlling the SDF</b>

14:50.990 --> 14:52.580
<b>As far as I can see...</b>

14:52.580 --> 14:56.080
<b>the media's divided in terms of tone.
That's because...</b>

14:56.580 --> 14:59.080
<b>they each have
different sources.</b>

15:00.620 --> 15:03.590
<b>Meaning that there are
two different forces behind the scenes?</b>

15:04.170 --> 15:09.590
<b>As you know, information gathering
isn't really the Jumonji Family's forte.</b>

15:09.590 --> 15:12.470
<b>I have no evidence to back up
what I'm about to tell you.</b>

15:12.470 --> 15:14.600
<b>Will you hear me out
without getting angry?</b>

15:15.890 --> 15:16.890
<b>Fine by me.</b>

15:16.890 --> 15:18.730
<b>Let me hear what you have to say.</b>

15:19.520 --> 15:25.230
<b>It's looking highly likely that the effort
to censure the JDF in the press...</b>

15:26.320 --> 15:29.240
<b>is secretly being driven
by the Saegusa Family.</b>

15:43.000 --> 15:47.590
<b>I do admit that my father is a tactician
who's fond of backroom maneuvering.</b>

15:47.590 --> 15:51.630
<b>And even I, his daughter, don't always
have a grasp on what he's thinking.</b>

15:52.430 --> 15:57.640
<b>But no matter what the reason, he's not one to forget
his duty as a member of the Ten Master Clans.</b>

15:58.180 --> 16:02.900
<b>There's no way he'd ever put Japan's
magic industry in an unfavorable position.</b>

16:03.520 --> 16:09.400
<b>Then, Mr. Saegusa must think this is
actually good for Japan's magic industry.</b>

16:09.990 --> 16:12.400
<b>What that may be, I have no clue.</b>

16:13.110 --> 16:14.490
<b>All I know is that...</b>

16:14.490 --> 16:19.790
<b>at a glance, Mr. Saegusa seems
to be betraying the Ten Master Clans.</b>

16:20.960 --> 16:22.750
<b>Fine, Jumonji.</b>

16:22.750 --> 16:25.000
<b>In that case, would you mind
coming over to my place?</b>

16:25.420 --> 16:27.170
<b>I'm going to ask my father directly.</b>

16:27.630 --> 16:29.510
<b>And I'd like you to be there.</b>

16:29.510 --> 16:30.840
<b>Fine.</b>

16:34.890 --> 16:37.260
<b>Thank you for making time
in your busy schedule...</b>

16:34.890 --> 16:37.260
<b>APRIL 19, A.D. 2096</b>

16:37.850 --> 16:39.520
<b>to see me.</b>

16:40.600 --> 16:43.230
<b>Well, it was at your request, Katsuto.</b>

16:43.600 --> 16:46.150
<b>So, what brings you here today?</b>

16:46.900 --> 16:47.900
<b>Right.</b>

16:48.230 --> 16:53.030
<b>Are you the one who's been inciting
the anti-magic press?</b>

16:54.110 --> 16:56.450
<b>Yes. Good job figuring that out.</b>

16:56.450 --> 16:58.910
<b>Father, how could you?</b>

16:59.830 --> 17:03.120
<b>Mayumi, why are you so flustered?</b>

17:03.620 --> 17:06.630
<b>By doing this, you've betrayed
the Ten Master Clans... no...</b>

17:07.210 --> 17:09.630
<b>the Japanese magic industry!</b>

17:09.630 --> 17:11.260
<b>Saegusa...</b>

17:20.760 --> 17:22.220
<b>Mr. Saegusa...</b>

17:22.220 --> 17:25.310
<b>I don't understand your thinking here.</b>

17:25.310 --> 17:27.980
<b>So, I'm asking you for an explanation.</b>

17:28.860 --> 17:31.980
<b>Are you asking me
as a member of the Jumonji Family?</b>

17:32.650 --> 17:35.240
<b>I'm asking you as a Jumonji.</b>

17:36.110 --> 17:38.950
<b>First off, I want to dispel
any misunderstanding.</b>

17:38.950 --> 17:40.740
<b>This campaign...</b>

17:41.080 --> 17:45.000
<b>was launched by a foreign
anti-magician faction.</b>

17:45.000 --> 17:48.500
<b>Not only did they feed stories
to the mass media...</b>

17:48.500 --> 17:51.130
<b>they're also funding them.</b>

17:51.960 --> 17:58.180
<b>So, does that mean that your intervention
in the press is a countermeasure?</b>

17:59.220 --> 18:01.010
<b>Absolutely.</b>

18:01.010 --> 18:03.640
<b>And unfortunately, just as they planned...</b>

18:04.350 --> 18:07.650
<b>the anti-magician movement
is about to become public sentiment.</b>

18:08.270 --> 18:15.440
<b>But as there's no specific spokesman
for public sentiment, it's not easy to refute.</b>

18:16.150 --> 18:17.150
<b>Katsuto...</b>

18:17.740 --> 18:22.660
<b>Do you know the most effective way
to counter public sentiment?</b>

18:23.330 --> 18:25.040
<b>To split it?</b>

18:25.620 --> 18:27.040
<b>That's correct.</b>

18:27.370 --> 18:29.960
<b>You can put out a fire faster...</b>

18:29.960 --> 18:34.300
<b>by dividing the coals into multiple small fires
before it turns into a single, large blaze.</b>

18:35.170 --> 18:37.840
<b>Small fires are better than a major blaze.</b>

18:38.340 --> 18:41.100
<b>I see. That's probably true.</b>

18:41.430 --> 18:42.050
<b>But...</b>

18:42.640 --> 18:45.980
<b>people can perish in small fires, as well.</b>

18:45.980 --> 18:48.440
<b>If they're not extinguished in time...</b>

18:48.440 --> 18:52.270
<b>a small fire can conceivably become
a fire that takes human lives.</b>

18:53.900 --> 18:56.070
<b>I'm speaking theoretically.</b>

18:57.030 --> 18:58.650
<b>It's mutual, sir.</b>

19:03.910 --> 19:05.290
<b>Mr. Saegusa...</b>

19:05.290 --> 19:10.420
<b>Regarding the Saegusa Family's manipulation of
the press, the Jumonji Family hereby requests...</b>

19:10.420 --> 19:14.920
<b>that you make your regret known and
immediately suspend your anti-magician campaign.</b>

19:17.010 --> 19:22.180
<b>The Saegusa Family hereby requests
a written petition from the Jumonji Family.</b>

19:22.180 --> 19:25.560
<b>I'd prefer to give my answer
after I've seen your official protest.</b>

19:26.890 --> 19:28.350
<b>Understood.</b>

19:28.350 --> 19:30.940
<b>I'll draw one up as soon as I return home.</b>

19:31.770 --> 19:36.150
<b>I'm sorry you had to make this trip today.</b>

19:45.990 --> 19:48.500
<b>Has Katsuto left?</b>

19:48.500 --> 19:49.460
<b>Yes.</b>

19:52.370 --> 19:55.420
<b>I can guess what it is
that you'd like to say.</b>

19:55.750 --> 19:57.050
<b>Go ahead and say it.</b>

19:58.010 --> 20:00.170
<b>What we just discussed...</b>

20:00.170 --> 20:03.930
<b>I feel that Jumonji's argument is sound.</b>

20:04.800 --> 20:08.890
<b>Mayumi, Master Kudou is also aware of this.</b>

20:08.890 --> 20:12.440
<b>He wasn't against my plan.</b>

20:13.310 --> 20:17.690
<b>I have no idea what the elderly master
may be thinking.</b>

20:17.690 --> 20:19.030
<b>All I know...</b>

20:19.320 --> 20:24.780
<b>is that it seems like a mistake to pointlessly
disrupt the lives of our fellow magicians...</b>

20:25.070 --> 20:27.540
<b>living in the same country.</b>

20:28.200 --> 20:32.290
<b>It's just to let them vent.
It'll be all over in a month at most.</b>

20:33.000 --> 20:38.670
<b>Even in a mere month, thoughtless slander
can inflict lifelong wounds in some cases!</b>

20:39.000 --> 20:39.920
<b>Mayumi...</b>

20:42.470 --> 20:45.680
<b>For whose sake are you so angry?</b>

20:45.680 --> 20:47.180
<b>Is it for Katsuto?</b>

20:48.010 --> 20:49.470
<b>Or is it for...</b>

20:49.470 --> 20:52.230
<b>someone at First High School?</b>

20:57.610 --> 20:59.190
<b><i>About that matter we discussed...</i></b>

20:59.780 --> 21:02.700
<b><i>Next Tuesday, April 24...</i></b>

21:03.200 --> 21:06.570
<b><i>a member of Parliament
will be visiting First High School.</i></b>

21:07.410 --> 21:09.740
<b>Would that be Congressman Kanda
of the Civil Rights Party?</b>

21:10.240 --> 21:11.370
<b><i>Yes.</i></b>

21:11.830 --> 21:15.620
<b><i>Apparently, he's going to crash First High
with his usual entourage of reporters.</i></b>

21:16.250 --> 21:18.130
<b>Crash and do what?</b>

21:19.040 --> 21:23.630
<b><i>He's probably going to try to point out
any collusion between First High and the military.</i></b>

21:24.510 --> 21:26.640
<b>But there is none.</b>

21:27.340 --> 21:32.890
<b><i>If he can't find any, he'll manufacture something by
cutting and pasting testimony and subjective comments.</i></b>

21:33.480 --> 21:35.900
<b><i>And his entourage of journalists...</i></b>

21:36.480 --> 21:39.110
<b><i>will embellish them ten times over...</i></b>

21:39.110 --> 21:41.900
<b><i>and will probably make a commotion
over them, don't you think?</i></b>

21:42.780 --> 21:45.650
<b>Right, I can see that happening.</b>

21:48.320 --> 21:50.490
<b>Thanks for reaching out.</b>

21:50.490 --> 21:52.580
<b>That's information I can use.</b>

21:52.580 --> 21:57.500
<b><i>I'm looking forward to seeing
how you deal with this.</i></b>

22:06.720 --> 22:10.600
<b><i>It looks like the time has come
to set that plan in motion.</i></b>

23:36.390 --> 23:40.020
<b>THE IRREGULAR
AT MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
DOUBLE SEVEN PART III</b>
